      "skill_id": "en-a2-002",
      "title": "Past continuous for ongoing and interrupted events",
      "explanation": "Use was or were plus the -ing form for an action that was in progress at a past moment: They were playing football. Use was with I, he, she and it and were with you, we and they. The past continuous often describes a longer action interrupted by a shorter one in the past simple, joined by when: I was cooking when the phone rang.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "I was cooking when the phone rang."
        },
        {
          "en": "They were playing football."
        },
        {
          "en": "What were you doing at eight o'clock?"
        }
      ],
