      "skill_id": "en-a2-003",
      "title": "Present perfect for experience and recent events",
      "explanation": "Form the present perfect with have or has plus the past participle: I have visited Paris. She has just finished. Use it for life experience and for recent events without a finished time. Frequent markers: ever (in questions), never, just, already, yet. Past participles: regular verbs add -ed; irregular ones must be learned (eaten, seen, been, gone). Do not use it with a finished time like yesterday.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "I have visited Paris."
        },
        {
          "en": "She has just finished."
        },
        {
          "en": "Have you ever eaten sushi?"
        }
      ],
