      "title": "Going to for plans and predictions",
      "explanation": "Use am, is or are plus going to and the base verb for plans and intentions: I am going to visit my aunt. Use it also for predictions based on what you can see now: Look at the clouds. It is going to rain. Questions put be first: What are you going to do? Do not drop be and do not add -s or -ing to the main verb.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "en": "I am going to visit my aunt."
        },
        {
          "en": "Look at the clouds. It is going to rain."
        },
        {
          "en": "What are you going to do?"
        }
